$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Synthesis of substituted 1,2,3-triazolylmethyl
carbazoles (4a-z and 4aa-ac). To a solution of alkyne 2 (0.7 mmol) and
azide (3a-z and 3aa-ac) (0.7 mmol), in t-butanol: water (1:1, v/v, 4 mL),
CuSO4•5H2O (20 mol%) and sodium ascorbate (20 mol%) were added. The
mixture was stirred at RT for 8-10 h. After completion (monitored by
TLC), the reaction mixture was diluted with ethyl acetate (20 mL) and
water (5 mL), and the organic layer was separated, washed with brine
solution, dried over anhydrous sodium sulphate and concentrated under
reduced pressure. The crude residue obtained was purified over silica gel
column chromatography to obtain corresponding 1,2,3-triazoles (4a-z and
4aa-ac).
9-((1-(2,5-Dimethylphenyl)-1H-1,2,3-triazol-4-yl)methyl)-9H-carbazole
(4l) Brown solid. m.p:130-132 °C; IR (KBr, cm-1): 3131 (C-H), 2921, 1530,
1450 (C-C), 1230, 1150, 830, 745; 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3): δ 8.11 (d, J =
7.7 Hz, 2H), 7.57-7.44 (m, 4H), 7.26 (t, J = 8.1 Hz, 4H), 7.13 (s, 2H),
6.97 (s, 1H), 5.74 (s, 2H), 2.27 (s, 3H), 2.03 (s, 3H); 13C NMR (75 MHz,
CDCl3): δ 140.0, 136.6, 131.0, 130.4, 126.2, 125.9, 123.0, 120.3, 119.4,
108.6, 38.8 (N-CH2), 20.5 (Ar-CH3), 17.2 (Ar-CH3); MS (ESI) m/z 353
(M+H)+; HR-MS (ESI) Calcd for C23H21N4 (M+H)+: 353.17607, found:
353.17703.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective, Huisgen cycloaddition
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Rational design, synthesis and evaluation of novel-substituted
1,2,3-triazolylmethyl carbazoles as potent inhibitors of Mycobacterium
tuberculosis
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Surineni, Goverdhan; Yogeeswari, Perumal; Sriram, Dharmarajan; Kantevari,
Srinivas
