$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Synthesis of substituted 1,2,3-triazolylmethyl
carbazoles (4a-z and 4aa-ac). To a solution of alkyne 2 (0.7 mmol) and
azide (3a-z and 3aa-ac) (0.7 mmol), in t-butanol: water (1:1, v/v, 4 mL),
CuSO4•5H2O (20 mol%) and sodium ascorbate (20 mol%) were added. The
mixture was stirred at RT for 8-10 h. After completion (monitored by
TLC), the reaction mixture was diluted with ethyl acetate (20 mL) and
water (5 mL), and the organic layer was separated, washed with brine
solution, dried over anhydrous sodium sulphate and concentrated under
reduced pressure. The crude residue obtained was purified over silica gel
column chromatography to obtain corresponding 1,2,3-triazoles (4a-z and
4aa-ac). 5-(4-((9H-carbazol-9-yl)methyl)-1H-1,2,3-triazol-1-yl) pentanol
(4aa) White solid. m.p:102-104 °C; IR (KBr, cm-1): 3126 (-OH), 2929,
1456, 1328, 1213, 1055 (C-O), 749, 722; 1H NMR (600 MHz, CDCl3): δ 8.11
(d, J = 7.5 Hz, 2H), 7.51-7.40 (m, 4H), 7.26 (t, J = 7.1 Hz, 3H), 5.64
(s, 2H of carbazole N-CH2), 4.18 (t, J = 6.7 Hz, 2H of triazole N-CH2),
3.54 (t, J = 6.0 Hz, 2H -CH2 of aliphatic C1), 1.87-1.73 (m, 2H -CH2 of
aliphatic C4), 1.60 (s, 1H of aliphatic-OH), 1.54-1.44 (m, 2H CH2 of
aliphatic C2), 1.33-1.25 (m, 2H -CH2 of aliphatic C3); 13C NMR (75 MHz,
CDCl3): δ 139.9, 125.9, 123.0, 121.2, 120.3, 119.3, 108.7, 62.2 (CH2 of
aliphatic C1), 50.1 (carbazole N-CH2), 38.8 (triazole N-CH2), 31.6 (CH2
of aliphatic C2), 29.7 (CH2 of aliphatic C4), 226 (-CH2 of aliphatic C3);
MS (ESI) m/z 335(M+H)+; HR-MS (ESI) Calcd for C20H23N4O(M+H)+: 335.18664,
found: 335.18637.
